Thanks to all who answered, the most complete answer was...

The file on the server the allows exporting the file system (or directory or
even file) is /etc/exports, see mountd(8) and exports(4).  The file on the
client that mounts everything at boot time is /etc/fstab, see mount(8) and
fstab(4).  Do "man -k nfs" also.

	-Ric Werme




